bedkar Rd, Byculla East","","","","","r","Established in 1855 as a treasure house of the decorative and industrial arts. This museum houses a large number of archaeological finds, maps and historical photographs of Mumbai, clay models, silver and copperware and costumes. Its…"],["Gloria Church","sight",18.975,72.83417,"Sant Savta Marg, Mustafa Bazar, Byculla West","","","","","r","This is one of the oldest Roman Catholic churches in Mumbai built by the Portuguese Franciscans in 1632. The present structure dates back to 1913. The grey stone steeple of the church rises to a height of 160 feet. It is the tallest…"],["Jerbai Baug and Rustom Baug","sight",18.97958,72.83863,"Victoria Rd, Mustafa Bazar","","","","","r","The two Parsi colonies where most of the Parsis of Byculla live."],["Magen David Synagogue","sight",18.96695,72.83222,"340 Sir J. J. Rd","","","","","r","Built in 1861 this is the first Bagdadi Jew Synagogue in Mumbai. The Bagdadi Jews started arriving in Mumbai (then Bomay ) in the early decades of the 19th century. During that time they are welcomed by the Bene Israel (Children of…"],["Magen Hasidim Synagogue","sight",18.97543,72.82705,"Morland Rd, Agripada","","","","","r","The Magen Hasidim Synagogue is the largest Bene Israel (Children of Israel) synagogue in Mumbai, it remains functional with a small congregation. The Bene Israel congregation of Mumbai (then Bombay) started in 1904. Initially they…"],["Veermata Jijabai Bhosale Udyan","sight",18.97811,72.83675,"Dr Babasaheb Ambedkar Rd, Byculla East","9AM–6PM (closed Wed); saplings are available from the Garden's Nursery. Thu–Tue 8AM–11AM and 3–5PM except on Sun and public holidays","","","","r","The zoo was established during British times and named \"Victoria Gardens\". After India's independence, the zoo is renamed after Shivaji's mother Jijabai, and is popularly known as Rani Baug (queen's garden). The place is not really…"],["Mazagaon Court","sight",18.96872,72.83585,"27, St Mary Rd, Tadwadi","","